Spec: SpecDD Language Validation

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Validate SpecDD `.sdd` files against known structure and section names.

Structure:
  ./SpecDDAnnotator.kt: IntelliJ annotator that turns validation issues into editor errors.
  ./SpecDDKnownSections.kt: Known section registry and typo suggestion support.
  ./SpecDDStructureValidator.kt: Text-level structure validation.
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.kt: Validation result and issue model.

Owns:
  ./validation.sdd
  ./SpecDDAnnotator.sdd
  ./SpecDDKnownSections.sdd
  ./SpecDDStructureValidator.sdd
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.sdd
  ./SpecDDAnnotator.kt
  ./SpecDDKnownSections.kt
  ./SpecDDStructureValidator.kt
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.kt

Can modify:
  ./validation.sdd
  ./SpecDDAnnotator.sdd
  ./SpecDDKnownSections.sdd
  ./SpecDDStructureValidator.sdd
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.sdd
  ./SpecDDAnnotator.kt
  ./SpecDDKnownSections.kt
  ./SpecDDStructureValidator.kt
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.kt

Can read:
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/parser/*
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/validation/*

Must:
  Validate known SpecDD section names.
  Report unsupported section names and likely section-name typos.
  Keep validation behavior independent from syntax highlighting.
  Use the shared `SpecDDLineClassifier` line classification boundary.
  Keep validation messages deterministic.
  Keep validation issue ranges precise enough for IntelliJ annotations.
  Use errors for validation diagnostics.
  Cover validation behavior with Kotest BehaviorSpec tests.

Must not:
  Define highlighting colors.
  Add user-facing settings or configuration UI.
  Implement syntax highlighting.
  Own section tokenization rules beyond consuming shared parser classifications.
  Change shared language facts from validation code.
  Report warnings for validation issues; validation diagnostics must be errors.
